--
-- THE TRANSFORM (eigen plane -> world plane). One affine map, no rotation,
-- no axis flip, so distances and bearings survive verbatim:
--   worldX = PLAZA_X + (ex - CENTER_EX) * STUDS_PER_UNIT
--   worldZ = PLAZA_Z + (ey - CENTER_EY) * STUDS_PER_UNIT
-- CENTER is the bounding-box center of the generated eigen centroids,
-- computed at load from the data, never hand-set. worldY is the plaza floor
-- (FLOOR_Y); the eigen plane is horizontal.
-- Units: STUDS_PER_UNIT = 20000, so 1 milli-eigen (0.001 eigen) = 20 studs.
-- NORTH: eigen -ey maps to world -Z (Roblox north), matching the HTML map's
-- bearing law (tools/cathedral_eigen_map.py bearing(): 0 = north, clockwise,
-- atan2(dx, -dy)). Distances in eigen units and bearings in degrees are
-- therefore THE SAME NUMBERS on the eigen plane as in the scan JSON, so the
-- walker overlay readout is directly checkable against the data file.
-- tools/eigenmap_overlay_check.py does exactly that: it loads THIS module
-- under the plain Luau CLI and diffs its math against the JSON.
-- To keep that possible, the pure-number API below never touches Roblox
-- globals; the Vector3 / Color3 adapters are separated at the bottom.

